      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_monitor",
        "description": "LM393 dual comparator monitors VCC_3V3 rail and generates POWER_GOOD signal. Comparator VCC (pin 8) powered from VCC_5V to ensure operation even if 3.3V rail fails. Channel 1 configuration: 1IN_P (pin 3) receives divided VCC_3V3 sense voltage; 1IN_N (pin 2) receives reference threshold voltage derived from VCC_5V via divider; when VCC_3V3 exceeds threshold, 1OUT (pin 1, open-drain) releases and external pull-up asserts POWER_GOOD high. Pull-up resistor on POWER_GOOD connects to appropriate logic rail based on downstream system requirements. Channel 2 unused: 2IN_P (pin 5) and 2IN_N (pin 6) both tied to GND per brief requirement; 2OUT (pin 7) left open.",
        "id": "power_monitor"
      },
